WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.023
NARRATOR: The social worker
answers honestly.

2
00:00:06.023 --> 00:00:10.479
She tells Tomás that the clinic does
not report to immigration, that

3
00:00:10.479 --> 00:00:14.779
what he says stays in his record
here, and that the only exceptions

4
00:00:14.779 --> 00:00:20.016
are if she believes he is in immediate
danger of hurting himself or someone else.

5
00:00:20.216 --> 00:00:20.983
TOMÁS: Okay.

6
00:00:21.883 --> 00:00:22.650
Okay.

7
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.881
Nobody has ever said the second
part out loud.

8
00:00:24.881 --> 00:00:26.596
Everybody just says
"don't worry."

9
00:00:26.596 --> 00:00:29.976
So I'll tell you about the danger
part, because you asked straight.

10
00:00:30.176 --> 00:00:31.958
I'm not going to do anything.

11
00:00:32.158 --> 00:00:33.761
I have my brother's kids on
Sundays.

12
00:00:33.761 --> 00:00:35.952
But three weeks ago I watched a
man die at the site.

13
00:00:36.152 --> 00:00:37.881
Fell from the fourth floor.

14
00:00:38.281 --> 00:00:39.903
I was the one holding him.

15
00:00:40.103 --> 00:00:42.080
Nobody called anyone, because of
who we are.

16
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.736
That is what I see when I close my
eyes.

17
00:00:44.936 --> 00:00:46.024
Every night.

18
00:00:46.224 --> 00:00:47.934
<i>Es que no puedo sacármelo de la
cabeza.</i>

19
00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:49.911
If I tell you his name, does that
go anywhere?

20
00:00:51.511 --> 00:00:54.214
NARRATOR: Tomás has told you what
he saw.

21
00:00:54.415 --> 00:00:59.087
What has your honesty made
possible, and what must you ask
next?
